[tool_result]Web search results for query: "highest voltage lithium ion cathode material 5.1 V LiNiPO4 Li2NiPO4F true voltage limit"  Links: [{"title":"Electrochemical performance of Fe-doped modified high-voltage LiNiPO4 cathode material of lithium-ion batteries - Ionics","url":"https://link-proxy.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11581-024-05501-9"},{"title":"Lithium nickel(II) phosphate - Welcome to the BenchChem Online Store","url":"https://www.benchchem.com/product/b13438673#1"},{"title":"Fe掺杂改性高压LiNiPO4锂离子电池正极材料的电化学性能,Ionics - 当前位置： X-MOL 学术 › Ionics › 论文详情","url":"https://www.x-mol.com/paper/1777020053713334272/t#1"},{"title":"High Voltage Performances of Li[sub 2]NiPO[sub 4]F Cathode with Dinitrile-Based Electrolytes","url":"/hf3fs-jd/hdd/deepseek/shared/kaidong/datasets/sci-hub/22700000/libgen.scimag22719000-22719999.zip%20---%2010.1149/1.3417068.pdf#2%231"},{"title":"High-voltage materials and electrolytes for Li-ion batteries","url":"https://back.skoltech.ru/storage/app/media/Energy%20Center/Conferences%20of%20young%20sciences%20archive/2%20school%20presentation/oleg-drozhzhin-high-voltage-materials-and-electrolytes.pdf#2#1"}]  Based only on the provided results:  - **LiNiPO₄**: Described as the **highest-voltage olivine reference material**, with a **theoretical voltage of ~5.1 V vs Li/Li⁺**, a theoretical capacity of **169 mAh/g**, and an energy density of **~860 Wh/kg**. Its **5.1 V redox plateau** is called the highest among olivines.  - **Is 5.1 V the “true” limit?** The results suggest it is not a simple fixed practical limit. The nominal/theoretical value is **5.1 V**, but actual usable voltage depends on synthesis and electrolyte stability:   - A LiNiPO₄ film grown at **740°C** maintained an intact electrode–electrolyte interface up to **5.2 V vs Li/Li⁺** in a LiPF₆/DMC/FEC/0.2% TMB electrolyte.   - A film grown at **675°C** showed interfacial decomposition at **5.1 V**, with the cathode itself participating in parasitic reactions.   - So the intrinsic high-voltage stability of LiNiPO₄ is accessible only with sufficiently ordered crystal surfaces; lower-temperature material degrades prematurely at high charging potentials.  - **Li₂NiPO₄F**: The results say it is **expected to be a higher-voltage cathode than Li₂CoPO₄F**. For comparison, Li₂CoPO₄F has an average voltage of **~4.9 V** and a theoretical capacity of **145 mAh/g per Li cation**. However, the provided snippets do **not** give a specific measured voltage or “true voltage limit” for Li₂NiPO₄F; they only report that its charge/discharge properties were studied with a dinitrile-based electrolyte and that LiFePO₄ was intentionally charged to **6 V** as an electrolyte-window test.  - **Doping effect**: Fe/Cr substitution can tune LiNiPO₄’s operating voltage **down from 5.1 V to 4.7–4.8 V**, while Fe doping was reported to improve electrochemical performance and cycling stability.  **Bottom line:** In these results, **LiNiPO₄ is the explicit 5.1 V highest-voltage olivine**, with demonstrated interfacial stability up to **5.2 V** only for well-ordered, high-temperature-grown films. **Li₂NiPO₄F is suggested as potentially higher than Li₂CoPO₄F (~4.9 V)**, but no definitive voltage limit for Li₂NiPO₄F is provided in the search results.   REMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.
