Volume=12&activeIssue=30#1"},{"title":"First-principles Study of Lithium Cobalt Spinel Oxides: Correlating - PDF Free Download - consisting of 16 f","url":"https://datapdf.com/first-principles-study-of-lithium-cobalt-spinel-oxides-corre583135669b793cfaf3aeb1bb713dec5a38537.html#3"}]  # LiCo₂O₄ Spinel Cathode Voltage in Lithium Batteries — Reported Values  Based on the search results, several studies report the electrochemical voltage behavior of LiCo₂O₄ spinel:  ## Experimental Voltage Profile (Choi & Manthiram, 2002, *J. Electrochem. Soc.*) - **Lithium extraction** from the **8a (tetrahedral) sites** occurs at around **3.8–4 V**. - **Lithium insertion** into the **16c (octahedral) sites** occurs at around **3.5–3.6 V**. - The experimentally observed **voltage difference of ~0.3 V** between the two processes is much smaller than the **1.3 V predicted by theoretical calculations** in the literature, and also smaller than the ~1 V observed for the LiMn₂O₄ system.  ## Structural/Electrochemical Study (2008, *J. Chil. Chem. Soc.*) - LiCo₂O₄ synthesized at 400 °C by thermal decomposition of nitrates; - Lithium **extraction occurred in the 3.2–3.8 V range**, while Li⁺ **insertion into the spinel lattice** was observed in the **2.00–2.25 V range**, with a diffusion coefficient D ≈ 8 × 10⁻¹⁶ cm² s⁻¹.  ## First-Principles Calculations (Li–Co spinel oxides study) - Calculated **GGA+U voltages** for layered (R-3̄m, HT-LCO) and spinel (Fd-3̄m, LT-LCO) LiCoO₂ charged to Li₀.₅CoO₂ are **3.58 V and 3.31 V** (vs. Li/Li⁺), respectively. - For the Fd-3̄m LT-LCO component, a **voltage hysteresis at ~3.7 V (charging) and ~3.5 V (discharging)** was observed, attributed in part to the formation of a metastable phase. - Extraction of Li⁺ from the **tetrahedral (Td) 8a site of LiCo₂O₄ occurs ~0.9 V higher** than from octahedral (Oh) sites.  ## Related Context - For LiCoₓMn₂₋ₓO₄ spinels, the Co³⁺/⁴⁺ redox in the spinel structure gives **~5 V plateaus** (e.g., LiCoMnO₄ shows rechargeable plateaus centered on 5.0 V). - A disordered spinel Li₂Co₂O₄ phase has been reported to form at the surface of LiCoO₂ cycled at 3.0–4.6/4.8 V. - In modified LiCoO₂ (LCO) cathodes, a coherent spinel LiₓCo₂O₄ surface coating contributed to improved high-voltage performance (2.8–4.6 V operation).  **In summary**, experimental reports place the main LiCo₂O₄ spinel redox activity at approximately **3.2–4 V** (with Li extraction at ~3.8–4 V and insertion at ~3.5–3.6 V in the most cited study), with a much smaller charge/discharge voltage separation (~0.3 V) than theory predicted.   REMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.
