t). - **General context**: vanadium polyanion compounds are known to exhibit a **~4 V insertion voltage** vs Li⁺/Li; e.g., LiV(HPO₃)₂ shows an average voltage of ~4.0 V for Li-ion batteries (ScienceDirect result).  **Bottom line:** The search results associate ~4.1 V (vs Li/Li⁺) with the two-Li plateau of Li₃V₂(PO₄)₃ and with a Li₃V₂(PO₄)₃-type impurity feature in LiVPO₄F₁₋ᵧOᵧ. In LiVPO₄F-type tavorites, the V³⁺/V⁴⁺ couple activates at high voltage in fluorine-rich compositions, while the average operating voltages reported for these oxy-fluorides are in the ~4.1–4.2 V range.   REMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.
